  "features": [
    {
      "area": "WS08 prime-field polynomial factorization",
      "implemented": "Complete bounded Berlekamp and positive-characteristic square-free factorization, including characteristic two and inseparable powers. Independent modular product reconstruction and typed proof-kernel Rabin irreducibility establish all factors and multiplicities.",
      "scope": "Univariate, degree <=64, prime <=65521, independent cumulative phase caps. Public factor/factor_list source composition independently reconstructs the original QQ expression before accepting modular results, binds every integer-component reduction, enforces the original canonical coefficient LCD and characteristic-coprime nonzero exterior content, and preserves the distinct pinned exterior conventions. Multivariate input, GF Poly objects, nonzero characteristic-divisible exterior content and exhausted work refuse. This does not embed QQ into F_p.",
      "regressions": "16 native tests include an exhaustive401-polynomial trial-division corpus, omitted/false factors, multiplicities, field/source/typed-coordinate mutations, coordinated exterior-content attacks and separate budget/cancellation failures."
    },
    {
      "area": "WS10 complete exact least-squares families",
      "implemented": "Minimum-norm X and complete orthogonal kernel projector P give all minimizers X+P*W for singular, rectangular and multi-RHS rational systems. Independent acceptance binds a complete original homogeneous affine witness and checks AP=0, symmetry, coverage of every kernel basis vector, all normal residuals and orthogonality of X.",
      "scope": "At most32 rows, unknowns and RHS columns,4096-bit input and8192-bit intermediate components; separate cumulative phase caps. Public pinv_solve and solve_least_squares(method=PINV) preserve fresh Dummy ownership, multi-RHS ordering, result classes and zero-area shapes. Original arbitrary-parameter forests are admitted before projection; held invalid children and changed accessors cannot hide behind zero projectors. In-process composite receipt."
    },
    {
      "area": "WS18 weighted geometric summation",
      "implemented": "Generate and independently coefficient-check q*P(k+1)-P(k)=p(k), then evaluate exact finite or convergent positive-infinite endpoints. Supports rational polynomial weights, signed/nonunit rational ratios, multiple geometric factors, affine integer exponents, symbolic integer endpoints and negative/reversed finite ranges.",
      "scope": "Degree <=32,4096 original nodes,depth64,4096-bit input rationals,20-million compute and128-MiB logical allocation per phase. Whole original syntax is admitted before zero shortcuts; operational/domain failures propagate. Positive-infinite nonzero sums require abs(q)<1. In-process receipt, not a new portable proof-kernel claim."
    },
    {
      "area": "WS19 complete rational coupled ODE systems",
      "implemented": "Independently verify Phi'=A*Phi and Phi(t0)=I for rational constant2x2 systems, covering all discriminant/Jordan/zero regimes. Exact general, partial and full rational initial coordinates are retained. Polynomial forcing uses an independently checked coefficient identity p'-A*p=b and constructs the complete family h+p-Phi*p(t0) without unchecked final simplification.",
      "scope": "Forcing degree <=16, particular degree <=18,1024-bit rational input components, independent cumulative200-million compute/512-MiB logical allocation phases. Python dsolve lowers the original two-equation source with an invertible rational derivative matrix, transforms the entire forcing vector and retains supplied function order and typed time. Nonlinear/variable-coefficient/nonpolynomial and unsupported boundary data refuse. In-process completeness receipts, not general ODE closure."
    },
    {
      "area": "Core exact arithmetic correctness",
      "implemented": "Retain coefficient times numeric remaining base when raw products enter additive collection. Sign-aware rendering flips only the first numeric factor accounted for by its enclosing minus.",
      "counterexample": "Before the fix, Mul[1,334/495]-1 incorrectly became0, x+Mul[-1,334/495] became x-1, and raw2*3 could contribute2. The shifted forced-ODE residual was the erroneous161/495.",
      "red_green_evidence": "All6 independent scalar/display regressions failed against unchanged production and pass after the two localized fixes. The original forced-ODE residual assertions were retained and now pass. Coverage includes all factor permutations, nested products,zero and exact1e-400 coefficients."
    }
